<article class="env-lemma" id="01AZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01AZ">Lemma <span data-tag="01AZ">17.6.3</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be the inclusion of a closed subset into the topological space $X$. The functor $\textit{Ab}(X) \to \textit{Ab}(Z)$, $\mathcal{F} \mapsto \mathcal{H}_ Z(\mathcal{F})$ of Remark <a href="/tag/01AY" data-tag="01AY">17.6.2</a> is a right adjoint to $i_* : \textit{Ab}(Z) \to \textit{Ab}(X)$. In particular $i_*$ commutes with arbitrary colimits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have to show that for any abelian sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $X$ and any abelian sheaf $\mathcal{G}$ on $Z$ we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\textit{Ab}(X)}(i_*\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F}) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\textit{Ab}(Z)}(\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{H}_ Z(\mathcal{F}))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       This is clear because after all any section of $i_*\mathcal{G}$ has support in $Z$. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>